pst-ks2: expose which sides of snapConnectBacker carry the retention
bumpouts as a `bumpoutSides` module parameter, so a use<>-ing model can
build the unidirectional "Wing Back" snap tiers (Moderate WB / Heavy WB)
from the same primitive as the bidirectional "Regular" snap.

The vendored QuackWorks connector library ships exactly one snap module,
snapConnectBacker, which hardcodes bumpouts on all four sides
([RIGHT, LEFT, FWD, BACK]) — i.e. Multiboard's bidirectional "Regular"
snap. There is no separate Wing-Back generator or parameter upstream.
Multiboard's taxonomy (libs/README.md "Multiboard constants") names two
further tiers — Moderate WB and Heavy WB — as *unidirectional* snaps
(retention on one axis so the part seats one way and resists pull-out).
The retention feature IS these green offset_sweep bumpouts, so limiting
them to one opposing pair converts the bidirectional snap into a
unidirectional wing-back one. Promoting the side list to a parameter is
the minimal, honest way to reach the tiers from the library primitive;
grip strength stays on the existing holdingTolerance knob.

Defaults to [RIGHT, LEFT, FWD, BACK], so the file's own top-level
Customizer call and the snap-regular variant render byte-for-byte as
before — no geometry change at default arguments.

